{"title":"Monday assorted links","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/952209374/0/marginalrevolution~Monday-assorted-links.html","date":1774888409000,"content":"<p>1. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.washingtonpost.com/nation/2026/03/27/cheesesteak-philadelphia-pats-king-of-steaks/\" target=\"_blank\">Was there a great Philadelphia cheese steak stagnation?</a></p>\r\n<p>2. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/29/opinion/free-speech-social-media-court-ruling.html\" target=\"_blank\">David French on the enemies of free speech</a> (NYT).  And <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/JMchangama/status/2038285693139493291\" target=\"_blank\">yes it is Indonesian censorship, nothing to celebrate</a>.</p>\r\n<p>3. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://aish.com/an-arab-zionists-harrowing-odyssey/\" target=\"_blank\">Profile of Hussein Aboubakr</a>.  Good piece on one of today’s best thinkers and writers.  Link to <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/HusseinAboubak\" target=\"_blank\">Twitter and Substack</a>.  Unlike many writers on these topics, it is not about your opinion of Israel, rather each piece is interesting and substantive.  Try his <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://critiqueanddigest.substack.com/p/the-years-of-crisis-and-decision?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=1991565&amp;post_id=192050918&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=false&amp;r=3o9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\">essay on Mahfouz</a>.</p>\r\n<p>4. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/tgof137/status/2038382566596829373\" target=\"_blank\">Lab Leak is somewhat declining in plausibility</a>.</p>\r\n<p>5. “China is cracking down on families who opt to bury their dead in empty high-rise properties — known as “bone ash apartments” — rather than pay skyrocketing costs for cemetery plots.” (<a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.ft.com/content/14ad5723-b97f-49d6-ab9e-265e4f7f0fff?accessToken=zwAAAZ0-u3KJkc8UrVcjuX9J1tOrniZeT38P_w.MEYCIQC_Wf3zRS6k_sSkL9zS-ZngrrIGU9jWU8NIJYL9zDnfAgIhANG6U00eDAmOpo5KCGsv1z5TQmcQ8OZF1q6aIDUa7Cbz&amp;sharetype=gift&amp;token=d4b503fe-3320-4ce9-846d-64674459a00a&amp;syn-25a6b1a6=1\" target=\"_blank\">FT</a>)</p>\r\n<p>6. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://nicholasdecker.substack.com/p/do-developing-countries-still-need?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=747616&amp;post_id=192552145&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=false&amp;r=3o9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\">Do developing countries still need to industrialize?</a></p>\r\n<p>7. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/JesusFerna7026/status/2038599152427311308\" target=\"_blank\">JFV on education and AI</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/03/monday-assorted-links-553.html\">Monday assorted links</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/952209374/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/952209374/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/952209374/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/952209374/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" sr